From: Maximilian Gaedig <sly-keg-cheating@duck.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845: drop gcc's CX power domain

The global clock controller is runtime-resumed for as long as any of its
clocks is prepared -- clk_core_prepare() holds a runtime-PM reference on
the provider -- and gcc always has ~40 prepared on a running system. As a
member of the cx genpd it is therefore permanently active, which makes
genpd_power_off(cx) impossible; and since rpmhpd's cx is not active_only,
to_active_sleep() mirrors the active corner into the RPMH_SLEEP_STATE
vote, so qcom_stats/cxsd stays pinned at 0 however idle the system gets.

Moving it to CX_AO fixes the sleep half but leaves a floor under
non-suspend idle: rpmhpd_aggregate_corner() folds max(peer->corner,
peer->enable_corner) into the shared cx.lvl ACTIVE vote for a merely
*enabled* peer, so a permanently-enabled cx_ao pins ACTIVE at
enable_corner (0x6 observed) even with cx and cx_ao both at perf 0. It
also reparents all 13 gdscs into cx_ao, which hold it enabled themselves.

gcc votes perf 0 either way, so dropping the domain costs no performance
state, only the enable-hold. On a OnePlus 6 (enchilada) cx_ao idle time
goes from 234 ms to 279451 ms and cx reaches off-0/perf 0 while awake
once the display controller and BT UART release it.

Signed-off-by: Maximilian Gaedig <sly-keg-cheating@duck.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi	2026-09-02 20:02:32.827007491 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi	2026-09-02 20:02:32.842999953 +0200
@@ -1244,7 +1244,37 @@
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 			#power-domain-cells = <1>;
-			power-domains = <&rpmhpd SDM845_CX>;
+			/*
+			 * Deliberately in no power domain.
+			 *
+			 * clk_core_prepare() takes a runtime-PM reference on
+			 * the provider for as long as a clock stays prepared,
+			 * and gcc always has ~40 prepared, so
+			 * 100000.clock-controller is permanently runtime-active
+			 * (usage=40, suspended_time=0). As a device inside the
+			 * cx genpd that makes genpd_power_off(cx) impossible,
+			 * and because rpmhpd's cx is not active_only,
+			 * to_active_sleep() mirrors the active corner into the
+			 * RPMH_SLEEP_STATE vote -- so qcom_stats/cxsd stayed
+			 * pinned at 0 no matter how idle the system got, with
+			 * every cx device suspended and perf=0.
+			 *
+			 * SDM845_CX_AO fixes that half (cx_ao is active_only,
+			 * so its sleep contribution is forced to 0) but leaves
+			 * a floor under non-suspend idle: rpmhpd_aggregate_corner()
+			 * folds in max(peer->corner, peer->enable_corner) for a
+			 * merely *enabled* peer, so a permanently-enabled cx_ao
+			 * pinned the shared cx.lvl ACTIVE vote at enable_corner
+			 * (observed 0x6) even with cx and cx_ao both at perf 0.
+			 * It also reparents all 13 gdscs into cx_ao, which then
+			 * hold it enabled on their own.
+			 *
+			 * gcc votes perf 0 in either arrangement, so dropping
+			 * the domain costs no performance state -- only the
+			 * enable-hold. Measured on OnePlus 6: cx_ao idle time
+			 * 234 ms -> 279451 ms, and cx reaches off-0/perf 0
+			 * while awake once the display and BT UART release it.
+			 */
 		};
 
